 "observations": [
  "body L3-L12: the derivation is right: in the right triangle FME, sin HEF : MF = sin FME : EF with FME = 90°; AM = AF cos HAF / R and MF = AF sin HAF / R with AF = e and HAF = m, both to the radius R of the sines; so EF = √[(e sin m / R)² + (e cos m / R + 60p)²], the denominator of p. 219.",
  "body L6, L18: within the root the print marks the segments MF and LE with a bar of their own under the bar of the root.",
  "body (figure): the figure is redrawn from the print: the eccentric about H and the concentric about E, of equal radii, and the seven straight lines, measured on the scan.",
  "body L15-L22: in the eccentric, LE = e sin m / R and LH = e cos m / R, and ME = √[LE² + (HL + 60p)²]; with the tangent, tang HEF = R · MF : (60p + AM) = R e sin m : (60p R + e cos m), and the same for tang LME, which is the formula of p. 219 in tangents.",
  "body L22, L24: «60pR» stands for 60p × R; with sines to the radius R = 60p the tangent of the equation is e sin m : (60p + e cos m / R) to the same radius, as printed.",
  "body L27: the fraction e/60 stands at the end of the line, as printed.",
  "body L29: in the head the dash after «g)» measures 9.8 pt and is transcribed as a dash; that of «17-20» measures 3.6 pt, a hyphen.",
  "body L33: the dash of «al–Battānī» is a long dash (5.3 pt)."
 ],
